---
// The page rule — the vertical line descending the page, in its final drawn state.
// motion-spec.md's initial-state pattern: markup ships every SVG finished; step 09 adds
// a scrub on `#rule path` on top of this, and must find the id and the path unchanged.
// Purely decorative — the real relationships (marker <-> note) already exist as real
// links in the markup, so this carries aria-hidden.
//
// `vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"` stays (step 09 tried removing it, then put it
// back — see below). The path's length is exactly 100 user units by construction
// (`d="M0.5 0 V100"`); motion.ts's tier1Rule() uses that fixed number directly and never
// calls DrawSVGPlugin on this element, so DrawSVGPlugin's own length-measurement code
// (which mis-scales a non-scaling-stroke path inside a non-proportional viewBox,
// DrawSVGPlugin.js:97-147) never runs against it. `.tick`'s path stays on DrawSVGPlugin,
// since a 1:1 viewBox is exactly the proportional case that plugin measures correctly.
---

<svg id="rule" class="rule-svg" viewBox="0 0 1 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
  <path
    d="M0.5 0 V100"
    fill="none"
    stroke="var(--color-line)"
    stroke-width="1"
    vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"
  />
</svg>
